        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0015772</oboInOwl:id>
        <ns3:IAO_0000115>The directed movement of oligosaccharides into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Oligosaccharides are molecules with between two and (about) 20 monosaccharide residues connected by glycosidic linkages.</ns3:IAO_0000115>
